  "full_prompt": "Create an animation introducing the fundamental ideas of calculus through the geometric problem of finding the area of a circle. Start by showing a circle with radius R and ask the question 'Why is area = πR²?' Then slice the circle into concentric rings, unwrap one ring to show it approximates a rectangle with width 2πr and thickness dr. Show the sum of all ring areas approximating the area under the graph of 2πr, which forms a triangle. Demonstrate that as dr approaches zero, the approximation becomes exact, yielding area = πR². Then introduce the area function A(x) for the parabola y = x², showing that dA/dx = x², and briefly introduce derivatives and the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.",
